Usage of resume:
  -budget float
    	alias for --call-budget (per call, not graph-wide) (default 0.25)
  -call-budget float
    	budget USD per call, not a graph-wide hard cap (default 0.25)
  -executor string
    	how workers are launched: herdr or local or tmux (default: the run's recorded executor, then IRRIGATOR_EXECUTOR, then local)
  -legacy-unbudgeted string
    	allow unbudgeted legacy runs to proceed without budget enforcement ('allow')
  -notify string
    	notify a phone or webhook when the run blocks, completes or a cell becomes uncertain or failed: ntfy, webhook or off (default: the run's recorded choice, then IRRIGATOR_NOTIFY_VIA, then off)
  -notify-topic string
    	ntfy topic for --notify ntfy (default IRRIGATOR_NTFY_TOPIC; the token is only read from IRRIGATOR_NTFY_TOKEN)
  -notify-url string
    	webhook URL for --notify webhook (default IRRIGATOR_APPROVALS_WEBHOOK)
  -retry-failed
    	retry replay-safe failed nodes
  -schedule string
    	opt-in ready order: breadth (roots before descendants) or depth (default); omitted keeps the run's saved order
  -session-registry string
    	absolute shared session registry v2 path (v1 migrates on next actual start; default ./.irrigator/current-session.json)
  -sizing string
    	opt-in sizing.v1 JSON enforced at admission; saved as RUN/sizing.json
  -timeout duration
    	timeout per call (default 2m0s)
  -workers int
    	maximum concurrent workers (default 2)
